From 02114f42d803e9d9e42a1304052646f7fca2e177 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Trung=20L=C3=AA?= <8@tle.id.au>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 17:36:07 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add little-endian PowerPC (ppc64le) support to VM JIT
 compiler

Make the JIT endian-independent, detect ELFv1/ELFv2 via _CALL_ELF and
follow each ABI's calling convention, fix a Z_Free of hunk memory and a
missing I-cache flush, add VSX variants of the AltiVec renderer and
sound paths, and fix two long-standing big-endian AltiVec bugs.

idppc is now set on ppc64le too, so keep the interpreter's lwbrx word
loads, which byte-swap, for big-endian only.

The VSX diffuse lighting ignores lane w of tess.normal, which the
scalar paths never write, and VectorArrayNormalize's PowerPC branches
process count entries like the generic one, instead of count + 1.
